NNAAMMEE
     rraaddiiuussdd__eeaapp22mmsscchhaapp — provides conversion from EAP-MSCHAPv2 to MSCHAPv2

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     rraaddiiuussdd__eeaapp22mmsscchhaapp

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The rraaddiiuussdd__eeaapp22mmsscchhaapp module is executed by radiusd(8) as an
     “authentication-filter” module to provide conversion from EAP-MSCHAPv2
     authentication messages to MS-CHAPv2 authentication messages.

CCOONNFFIIGGUURRAATTIIOONNSS
     The rraaddiiuussdd__eeaapp22mmsscchhaapp module supports the following configuration key
     and value:

     cchhaapp--nnaammee _n_a_m_e
             Specify the name in CHAP.  The default is “radiusd”.

FFIILLEESS
     /usr/libexec/radiusd/radiusd_eap2mschap  “eap2mschap” module executable.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     An example showing the rraaddiiuussdd__eeaapp22mmsscchhaapp module providing an authentica‐
     tion server that supports EAP-MSCHAPv2.  Although the radiusd_file(8)
     module itself doesn't support any EAP methods, when used with the
     rraaddiiuussdd__eeaapp22mmsscchhaapp module it becomes possible to support EAP-MSCHAPv2.

     _/_e_t_c_/_r_a_d_i_u_s_d_._c_o_n_f:

           listen on 192.168.0.1
           client 192.168.0.0/24 {
               secret SECRET
           }

           module file {
               set path "/etc/npppd/npppd-users"
           }
           module eap2mschap

           authentication-filter * by eap2mschap
           authenticate * by file

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     authenticate(3), radiusd.conf(5), radiusd(8), radiusd_file(8)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The rraaddiiuussdd__eeaapp22mmsscchhaapp module first appeared in OpenBSD 7.6.

